<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Democratic Progressive Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1986">1986</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as DPP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Democratic Progressive Party is a Taiwanese political party founded on 28 September 1986, while martial law was still in force, by opponents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a> one-party rule. It campaigned for democracy and a distinct Taiwanese identity. It won the presidency under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-shui-bian">Chen Shui-bian</a> in 2000 and again under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsai-ing-wen">Tsai Ing-wen</a> in 2016 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lai-ching-te">Lai Ching-te</a> in 2024.</p></div>
